WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.942
Moving Group Policy to Intune changes the
baseline of every device, so the plan,

3
00:00:06.942 --> 00:00:12.615
the library and the sync record are
evidence for NIST special publication eight

4
00:00:12.615 --> 00:00:17.188
hundred fifty-three's
configuration-management controls: C M two,

5
00:00:17.188 --> 00:00:21.761
baseline configuration, C M three,
configuration change control,

6
00:00:21.761 --> 00:00:25.825
and C M six, configuration settings,
with C A seven and A C six.

7
00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:33.650
VK-INT-07's results show every in-scope
GPO imported and ready, or listed.

8
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.382
The move plan, saved
with the pull request,

9
00:00:36.382 --> 00:00:40.238
gives each setting a disposition
and shows the conflicts.

10
00:00:40.238 --> 00:00:45.000
The library and its decision records give
one owner and one decision per setting.

11
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
The sync record shows what
the sync would create,

12
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.525
then wrote only that, with a
read-only scope for the dry run.

13
00:00:51.525 --> 00:00:56.337
A library that differs from the tenant
stops the release, and the run log shows it.

14
00:00:56.337 --> 00:00:59.824
And Microsoft's sample is
pinned and its behavior tested.

15
00:00:59.824 --> 00:01:04.758
The Key Security Indicators come from
FedRAMP's Consolidated Rules for 2026:

16
00:01:04.758 --> 00:01:07.996
they're FedRAMP 20x
indicators for providers,

17
00:01:07.996 --> 00:01:10.925
and the agency lines its
evidence up with them.

18
00:01:10.925 --> 00:01:14.540
Which output supports which
control is this workbook's reading.
